  "insights": [
    {
      "id": "ins-sury",
      "status": "published",
      "tag": "Forced Labor",
      "sev": "warn",
      "place": "Ahmedabad, IN",
      "jurisdiction": "IN",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T08:00:00Z",
      "author": "R. Iyer",
      "sourceCount": 15,
      "subjectId": "sury",
      "cardTitle": "UK buyer's solar module supplier is 62% owned by a BVI holding with nominee directors",
      "title": "UK Buyer's Solar Module Supplier Is 62% Owned By A BVI Holding With Nominee Directors",
      "dek": "Suryadeep Photovoltaics, which ships solar modules to Grantham Electrical Manufacturing under a five-year contract signed in March 2024, is 62% owned by Tarnwell Holdings, a British Virgin Islands company whose filed directors are nominees. Tarnwell's own owners are a Cayman trust and a Hong Kong investor who once sat on the board of Suryadeep's former polysilicon supplier.",
      "paras": [
        "Tarnwell Holdings took its 62% stake in March 2022, according to Suryadeep's annual return with India's Ministry of Corporate Affairs. Managing director Rajiv Menon holds a further 18%. Tarnwell's register of members, exhibited in Hong Kong court proceedings in 2024, lists two holders: Larchmere Trust in the Cayman Islands with 45%, and Wei-Lun Cheung with 55%.",
        "Cheung was a director of Sino-Indo Polysilicon Trading FZE until November 2022. The Dubai trader supplied Suryadeep's polysilicon until May 2023 and has drawn adverse media over where that polysilicon came from. Suryadeep's current inputs, including glass from its Kalinga joint venture, carry no flags.",
        "Analyst view: on the record, 27.9% of Suryadeep traces through a trust whose settlor is not disclosed. That is below a control test but above the 25% beneficial-ownership threshold most buyer screens apply. The open question for Grantham is who stands behind Larchmere."
      ],
      "versions": [
        "v1",
        "v2",
        "b1",
        "v3",
        "v4"
      ]
    },
    {
