      ],
      "cardTitle": "Grantham's solar supplier traces back to a sanctioned Xinjiang defense group through its majority owner",
      "title": "Grantham's Solar Supplier Traces Back To A Sanctioned Xinjiang Defense Group Through Its Majority Owner",
      "dek": "Suryadeep Photovoltaics, which has supplied Grantham Electrical Manufacturing since March 2024, is 62% owned by Tarnwell Holdings. The Cayman trust that holds 45% of Tarnwell was settled by a Xinjiang university whose joint laboratory partner, Tianshan Aerospace & Defence Electronics, is on the US Entity List and wholly owned by an OFAC-designated state corporation.",
      "paras": [
        "Grantham buys solar modules from Suryadeep under supply agreement GEM-2024-117, a five-year term signed on 14 March 2024. Suryadeep is not listed itself, and no listed party appears in its shipments. Grantham's exposure runs through ownership: 27.9% of its supplier traces to a trust settled by a university with a defense partner.",
        "Tarnwell Holdings, registered in the British Virgin Islands, took 62% of Suryadeep in March 2022. Larchmere Trust holds 45% of Tarnwell. A deed of settlement exhibited in Hong Kong court proceedings names Xinjiang Polytechnic University of Materials Science and Engineering as the trust's settlor in June 2020, and the university's own accounts refer to an overseas education endowment.",
        "Since 2019 the university has run a joint laboratory with Tianshan Aerospace & Defence Electronics, which was added to the US Entity List in April 2021. Tianshan is wholly owned by Xinjiang Production Zone Development Corp., designated by OFAC in December 2020, so under OFAC's 50 Percent Rule Tianshan's property is blocked as well.",
        "Analyst view: a settlor holds no shares, so the chain does not meet an ownership test. It does put a listed defense contractor four Links above a UK buyer's supplier, close enough that Grantham's next supplier attestation will have to address it."
      ],
